1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,660
Does this mean I managed to make the world a peaceful place?

2
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:17,320
Oh, cool. You're already awake. Good morning, big brother.

3
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:23,380
Coterie, you're all right. What about Fraxinus? How's the crew? Is everyone okay?

4
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,080
Is it possible you're still asleep?

5
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:29,380
Uh, no, I'm... Hold on. What day is it?

6
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:32,640
Huh? It's the 3rd of November, don't you know that?

7
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:37,400
If it's November 3rd, then... It's the day after Origami went inverse.

8
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,700
Thank goodness. What a relief.

9
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:43,540
What the heck? What's happening?

10
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:47,260
I did it. I managed to change the world after all.

11
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:57,900
Daily life. On the surface, we think we know what it is.

12
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:02,500
Then, reality rears its head, and we discover all is not as it seems.

13
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,380
No way.

14
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,300
Well, it reminds me as follows.

15
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:05,800
Nah.

16
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:14,920
I want to see...

17
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:44,900
We'll be right back.

18
00:01:44,920 --> 00:02:14,900
We'll be right back.

19
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:44,900
We'll be right back.

20
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:49,020
Isn't that what you said you'd make yesterday, or am I not remembering right?

21
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:49,700
Yesterday?

22
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:52,240
Oh, right, I did.

23
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,080
Sorry.

24
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:55,140
Didn't end up having those ingredients.

25
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:57,820
So I made you a rice bowl.

26
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,240
With sweet eggs, too.

27
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,280
Oh, my God.

28
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:03,140
That sounds so good right now.

29
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:04,900
Oh, I mean, I literally...

30
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:08,160
Does this world have a whole different history that I'm not aware of?

31
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,480
Well, what a nice morning.

32
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:13,060
It was good of you to pick me up, servant.

33
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:14,440
Salutations.

34
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:15,560
Good morning, everyone.

35
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:17,660
Shido, Toka, Coterie.

36
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:18,720
Yeah, hey.

37
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:19,580
Morning.

38
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:23,300
What's with you?

39
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:28,000
If I didn't know better for a second there, I would have sworn you were totally checking out our boobs.

40
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:28,820
Explanation.

41
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:31,980
While gross, it still isn't an unheard of reaction for a man.

42
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:34,000
Care to add anything, Shido?

43
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:34,320
Nope.

44
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:35,000
I'm good.

45
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:35,440
Thanks.

46
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:44,000
Origami hasn't shown up yet.

47
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:48,480
Uh, what's the matter?

48
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:49,640
I don't know.

49
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:50,880
I can't explain it.

50
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:52,600
It's as if something is incomplete.

51
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:54,580
Just kind of a weird feeling.

52
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:55,960
Incomplete?

53
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:57,640
Welcome.

54
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:58,820
Good morning, everyone.

55
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:01,060
Suzuhara?

56
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:01,700
Here.

57
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:03,100
Satoshi?

58
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:03,940
Here.

59
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,080
Is she absent today?

60
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:05,800
Here.

61
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,100
Or maybe she's just running late.

62
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,820
Next is Tonomachi?

63
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:10,660
Yo!

64
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:15,380
Hiroto Tonomachi is present and accounted for and ready to face the day, my love.

65
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:15,680
Right.

66
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,940
So, Tonomachi is very much present.

67
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,340
Next is Nakahara?

68
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:19,600
Huh?

69
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:20,980
What's wrong?

70
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:23,780
Did I say something weird or are you just having a moment?

71
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,100
Um, no, I'm...

72
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:28,060
Her name should come after Tonomachi's.

73
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:30,520
Sorry, but what about Origami?

74
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:32,220
Who's Origami?

75
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:35,820
I don't think I've ever known anyone by that name.

76
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:36,420
Huh?

77
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:38,060
Origami?

78
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,860
What the heck kind of name is that?

79
00:04:40,340 --> 00:04:43,300
What, did Itsuka, like, fold a bunch of paper cranes for the teacher?

80
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:43,880
Ugh!

81
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:47,160
Hold on, does he think you can steal my Tammy with arts and crafts?

82
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,720
That's so lame.

83
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,120
Oh, I see.

84
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:55,060
I guess, here in this reality, Origami doesn't live in the city.

85
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:59,260
The Origami of this world probably doesn't hold a grudge against spirits.

86
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,640
She's just off somewhere living happily with her parents.

87
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:04,900
It's better this way.

88
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:06,820
This is how it always should have been.

89
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:08,020
Shiro?

90
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:10,120
What's up, Toka?

91
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,000
Are you alright?

92
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:13,880
Is something bothering you?

93
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,400
Oh, no, I'm fine.

94
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:24,000
I hope that she's happy.

95
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:29,160
Though, I would have loved to see her again, even just once.

96
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:33,060
To see this new Origami, smiling.

97
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:41,160
What's going on?

98
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:42,120
Is he okay?

99
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,640
Yeah, seems like he's in the dumps.

100
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,520
Look at how zoned out he is.

101
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:47,660
Has to be a girl.

102
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:49,320
What do you mean?

103
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:50,240
Why do you think that?

104
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:53,180
I mean, I might be wrong, so don't get your panties all in a twist.

105
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,980
Hey, if you know, out with this!

106
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:57,660
It's just that when it comes to the troubles of high school boys,

107
00:05:57,740 --> 00:06:00,080
you can lay money down on it being about some girl.

108
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:03,220
Someone treating them badly or not reciprocating their feelings.

109
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:06,200
Typical guys worry about these things all the time.

110
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:06,960
Really?

111
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:08,720
They worry about that stuff, too?

112
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:12,040
Yeah, even though when you ask if they want to group up for a project,

113
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:14,660
they say, ew, and try to act all disgusted.

114
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,260
And when you pick up their eraser,

115
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,480
they say you can just keep it now that you've touched it or something dumb.

116
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,100
Hold on, back up a minute.

117
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:24,740
How the heck does a spirit like you know so much about student life anyway?

118
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:26,540
Uh, listen.

119
00:06:26,940 --> 00:06:29,880
The point is, I think it's obvious that something happened to him at school.

120
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:33,620
He'll probably be fine if we give him time, but I can't help but worry.

121
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:36,260
Me too.

122
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:39,080
It's tough seeing Shido acting so depressed like this.

123
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:41,080
Isn't there anything we can do for him?

124
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:42,500
I don't know what to tell you.

125
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:44,300
I'll say one thing.

126
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:46,420
If it's girl trouble that's giving Shido grief,

127
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:48,740
then the only thing to heal his heart is another girl.

128
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:54,000
Oops, too close.

129
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,660
Man, I'm kind of focused.

130
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:56,740
Hey, Shido.

131
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,060
Need some help?

132
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:58,380
Huh?

133
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,040
Sure, thank you.

134
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:01,440
Why don't you wash...

135
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:05,420
What kind of outfits are those?

136
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,200
And what's with those bodies?

137
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:07,640
What?

138
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:08,740
We all have a body.

139
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:09,480
What's the problem?

140
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:11,140
Yeah, she's right.

141
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:12,920
Don't think about that right now.

142
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:14,540
What's important is that we help.

143
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:15,260
Right?

144
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:17,640
It's just that, um...

145
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:18,100
Patsumi!

146
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:19,600
Was this your idea?

147
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:21,060
Maybe it was.

148
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,060
Maybe it wasn't.

149
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:23,480
Wait a damn second.

150
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:25,900
Why aren't you in a bathing suit like the two of us?

151
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:28,360
I thought we all agreed that we'd get dressed up together.

152
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:29,860
It's true, we did.

153
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:33,600
But once I thought about it, I realized that wearing that would be super embarrassing.

154
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:35,980
I was afraid I might feel stupid, you know?

155
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:38,580
Girl, you're the one who gave us these stupid outfits!

156
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:39,840
You little...

157
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:40,460
Get over here!

158
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:42,560
I'll dress you myself to calm down!

159
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,960
I'm being violated!

160
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:46,320
You guys!

161
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:47,980
Would you please knock it off?

162
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:48,740
Huh?

163
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:55,380
Uh, pal, that was rough.

164
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:56,360
Everyone good?

165
00:07:56,360 --> 00:08:03,180
You guys are killing me, you know?

166
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,940
Well, I'm sorry about that.

167
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,480
I apologize, Shido.

168
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:08,420
Yeah, sorry.

169
00:08:08,940 --> 00:08:09,640
No worries.

170
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:11,760
I'm sorry that I had you all concerned.

171
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:12,900
Thank you.

172
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,580
I really am better now.

173
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:19,860
I don't mean to pry into your business or anything, but man, get a hold of yourself.

174
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:23,620
After all, you never know when another spirit is going to appear, right?

175
00:08:24,060 --> 00:08:24,500
Yeah.

176
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:26,920
There are spirits we don't know about.

177
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:29,900
Not to mention the fact that Kurumi and Devil are out there.

178
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:30,960
Wait, who's Devil?

179
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:32,280
I don't know that spirit.

180
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:34,300
What are you talking about?

181
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:36,360
I mean the spirit hunter, Devil?

182
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:41,260
And if you thought that Nightmare was bad, this one can be every bit as dangerous.

183
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:43,220
As bad as Kurumi?

184
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:45,100
Are you for real right now?

185
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:47,040
What the heck's with you today, Shido?

186
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:50,360
It's almost as if you've forgotten everything up until yesterday.

187
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:51,520
Sorry.

188
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:53,580
Could she go over some info again?

189
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:55,880
The stuff about this spirit named Devil.

190
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,160
Fine.

191
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:04,600
We've confirmed she exists, but she's an unidentified spirit who's evaded all attempts at contact so far.

192
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:08,640
Also, not surprisingly, I'd say, Devil's an inverse.

193
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:10,660
Wait, what do you mean?

194
00:09:11,020 --> 00:09:13,900
An inverse spirit just shows up here sometimes?

195
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:15,940
Well, I'm trying to tell you.

196
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,680
We don't know very much about her yet.

197
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:18,940
Tell me this, though.

198
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:20,200
What's a spirit hunter?

199
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:22,100
It's just like it sounds.

200
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:24,620
Devil never shows up anywhere on her own.

201
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:28,660
She only appears whenever another spirit manifests itself.

202
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:31,320
Then, suddenly, she's there and she attacks them.

203
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:36,220
If Toka and the others hadn't helped her out, Natsumi would have been in big trouble.

204
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:37,920
Wait a minute.

205
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:38,920
Is this her?

206
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:40,040
Yeah.

207
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,980
Horikami.

208
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:42,060
Horikami.

209
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:52,660
Shido, are you still sleepy?

210
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:54,300
No, I'm okay.

211
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:56,900
I just didn't get much rest last night.

212
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:58,000
Oh.

213
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:03,780
Where is Horikami?

214
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,520
She wasn't in her apartment.

215
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:09,960
And she wasn't at the house where she lived with her parents, either.

216
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:13,100
Why did she become a spirit?

217
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:14,460
Why an inverse?

218
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:20,340
By changing history five years ago, I should have saved her mom and dad.

219
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:21,560
Good morning, everybody.

220
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:22,900
I have an idea.

221
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:24,520
Let's go all out today.

222
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,580
What happened during that five-year span?

223
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:28,140
What could have changed?

224
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:29,800
Oh, I almost forgot.

225
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,880
I can't do much alone.

226
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:36,240
Maybe if I explain what I know, Ratatasker will look into it.

227
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:41,020
If I could have your attention, today I have a new friend to introduce to you all.

228
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:41,760
Go ahead.

229
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:42,700
Come on in, please.

230
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:51,680
I'm Horikami Tobiiichi.

231
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:52,520
Hello.

232
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,380
It's nice to meet you, everyone.

233
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:57,740
Look at that dazzling long hair and that pure, innocent smile.

234
00:10:58,280 --> 00:11:01,040
She's cute enough to give my honey a run for her money.

235
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,400
Well, let's see.

236
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:05,000
It looks like the seat next to Itsuka is open.

237
00:11:05,420 --> 00:11:06,780
Please feel free to sit there.

238
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:07,660
Sure, thanks.

239
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:11,040
No way.

240
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,500
Don't I know you?

241
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:18,940
What do you mean?

242
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,900
What makes you think Devil transferred to your school?

243
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:24,400
I'll explain it later, once I'm back home.

244
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,000
I swear it's true.

245
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:27,620
You have to believe me.

246
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:28,420
All right.

247
00:11:28,420 --> 00:11:31,060
But I admit, I'm not thoroughly convinced.

248
00:11:31,380 --> 00:11:32,080
I get it.

249
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:34,140
I'll have Ratatasker investigate.

250
00:11:34,140 --> 00:11:36,160
What's the student's name?

251
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:37,480
Origami.

252
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,540
Last name Tobiiichi.

253
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:40,580
Hold on.

254
00:11:40,580 --> 00:11:43,520
Do you mean Origami Tobiiichi from the AST?

255
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:44,480
Wait.

256
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:47,620
Coterie, do you remember the last world?

257
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:48,960
What are you talking about?

258
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:53,020
I know her because she fought against Toka and the others a bunch of times.

259
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:55,600
She retired not too long ago.

260
00:11:56,220 --> 00:12:03,260
Now that you mention it, it does seem like Tobiiichi left the AST around the same time Devil first started appearing regularly.

261
00:12:03,820 --> 00:12:05,800
Why did Origami join the AST?

262
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:07,820
I saved her parents.

263
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:08,920
Are you even listening?

264
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:10,560
Sorry, yeah.

265
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:12,860
Just tell me if you find out anything.

266
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:17,500
I don't get it.

267
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:20,920
If I changed what happened five years ago, then why would she...

268
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:25,020
Guess I'm gonna have to ask her in person.

269
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:36,280
Was this for me?

270
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:38,640
Did you want to talk about something?

271
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:39,520
Yeah.

272
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:41,220
Sorry to bother you, Origami.

273
00:12:41,460 --> 00:12:41,960
Thank you.

274
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:43,560
Oops.

275
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:44,480
Sorry.

276
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:45,700
We haven't met yet.

277
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:48,720
I guess it's kind of rude to talk as if I know you.

278
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:49,420
No.

279
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,820
I just wasn't expecting my first name.

280
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:52,840
And you're...

281
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:54,300
Itsuka, right?

282
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:57,000
What is this about?

283
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:58,400
A question.

284
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:02,060
When you saw me this morning, did you try to ask me something?

285
00:13:02,580 --> 00:13:02,880
Oh.

286
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:05,400
Sorry if that's been bothering you.

287
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:07,600
It's just that I was a little surprised.

288
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:11,320
The thing is, you look just like someone I met a long time ago.

289
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:15,300
You mean, could we have...

290
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:17,700
No, I don't think we've met.

291
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:21,160
The person I'm referring to I saw around five years ago.

292
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:23,880
You would have been in elementary school.

293
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:25,080
Besides.

294
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,560
That person actually passed away.

295
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,160
Five years ago.

296
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:31,960
Right before my eyes.

297
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:33,940
Oh my gosh.

298
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:35,980
She means me.

299
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:38,980
So, shouldn't we go back to class now?

300
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:40,320
Uh, wait.

301
00:13:40,580 --> 00:13:41,280
Hold on a sec.

302
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:43,840
Five years ago.

303
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:47,640
This didn't happen during the Nanko area fire, did it?

304
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,280
How did you know that?

305
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:50,580
Oh gosh.

306
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,880
Could that have been your older brother that I saw that day?

307
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:55,860
Well, something like that.

308
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:00,240
What is it?

309
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:04,640
Oh, I owe him everything.

310
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:07,420
Your brother saved both of my parents' lives.

311
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:12,120
If he hadn't been there, my mom and dad would have both died for sure.

312
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,360
I'm forever grateful.

313
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:15,540
Oh, sure.

314
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:17,940
That confirms it.

315
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:21,380
Sounds like I was able to save Origami's parents after all.

316
00:14:21,380 --> 00:14:25,080
Ah, sorry for blurting that out.

317
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:27,140
No, it's okay.

318
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:30,420
I am so thankful for what he did for them that day.

319
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:35,620
Even though, as fate would have it, my parents then died in a car accident a year later.

320
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:36,620
No.

321
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:41,340
But thanks to your wonderful brother, that last year they were alive,

322
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:44,400
my mom and dad were able to give me so much love and happiness.

323
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:46,860
Wow, I'm glad.

324
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:49,000
Is that the hand of fate at work?

325
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:50,660
Are you okay?

326
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:54,620
Well, I was kind of wondering why you joined the AST.

327
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:56,700
I mean, since they survived.

328
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:59,000
Wait, how did you know about that?

329
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:01,420
Oh, I don't know. I just, uh...

330
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:02,660
Did you go outside?

331
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,920
In the middle of a spatial quake alarm?

332
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:06,920
You know you're not allowed to do that.

333
00:15:07,140 --> 00:15:09,140
Uh, yeah. That's what I did.

334
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:10,480
That's very dangerous.

335
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,380
You always have to evacuate.

336
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:13,860
Right, sure.

337
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:19,120
Would you like to know the reason I joined the AST?

338
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:20,780
I would.

339
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:23,340
But only if you don't mind telling me.

340
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:30,600
So, the fact that you know about the AST has to mean that you know the reason for the alarms in the first place.

341
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:31,460
The spirits.

342
00:15:31,460 --> 00:15:36,860
During the fire five years ago, it was actually a spirit that killed your older brother.

343
00:15:37,220 --> 00:15:38,720
But that was...

344
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,640
I kept thinking.

345
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:42,960
I didn't want more people to have to suffer the way he did.

346
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:47,380
I wanted to become a person who could protect others from spirits.

347
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:52,440
She did this because of me.

348
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:58,540
Can I ask you one more thing?

349
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:00,220
Yes, of course.

350
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:04,380
I'm just wondering why you became a spirit.

351
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:05,280
Huh?

352
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:06,960
What are you talking about?

353
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:10,040
What does this mean?

354
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:12,040
That had to be...

355
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:13,720
Sounds like lunchtime's about over.

356
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:15,840
Thanks so much, Itsuka.

357
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,480
I'm glad we were able to chat like this.

358
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,000
Hold on!

359
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,820
Can we talk a little bit more?

360
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:24,000
But I think class is about to start.

361
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,520
Some other day is fine.

362
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:28,340
If you're free sometime, can I see you?

363
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:29,220
Huh?

364
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:30,760
Like on a date?

365
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:32,500
Uh, yeah.

366
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:33,820
I guess so.

367
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:34,780
Thank you.

368
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:37,360
Do you think I could have some time to think about it?

369
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,280
Uh, yeah, of course.

370
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:41,300
Thanks.

371
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,660
Goodbye, then.

372
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:48,120
So strange, talking to her now.

373
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:51,280
Am I too used to the other Hurekami?

374
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:55,380
Shido.

375
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:58,200
Where the heck did you disappear to during lunch?

376
00:16:58,540 --> 00:17:00,540
Oh, I just got a call from Coterie.

377
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:02,200
She's fine with curry for dinner.

378
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:04,260
Ah, that's terrific news.

379
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:05,780
My mouth's already watering.

380
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:17,780
Saturday, huh?

381
00:17:19,820 --> 00:17:22,020
Guess I need to have that talk with Ritatusker.

382
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:29,340
Oh, I'm so tired.

383
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:29,840
I'm so tired.

384
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,380
I'll just rest a bit.

385
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:43,420
My goodness.

386
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:44,300
Huh?

387
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:47,680
Big boys like you should watch where they sleep.

388
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:49,200
Dear Shido.

389
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:49,880
Kurumi!

390
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:52,120
Kurumi!

391
00:17:53,220 --> 00:17:54,360
Last I checked.

392
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:56,260
Well, that was quite the greeting, wasn't it?

393
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:59,080
Who knew you had such a cute little sleeping face?

394
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,560
Uh-oh.

395
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:03,480
What's wrong?

396
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:07,640
You know, I'm honestly, deeply hurt that you seem to fear me so much.

397
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:12,240
And here I thought we were comrades who were changing the world together.

398
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:14,100
Kurumi, do you?

399
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:15,600
Yes.

400
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:17,500
I remember everything.

401
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:19,580
All about the original world.

402
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:21,500
And about origami, too.

403
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:22,800
Oh, good.

404
00:18:23,580 --> 00:18:25,660
Then tell me, why did things end up this way?

405
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:27,920
What happened to origami in this world?

406
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:30,840
I'm afraid that's something even I'm not aware of, Shido.

407
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:37,840
However, with origami the way she is now, there are definitely certain ways for us to find out.

408
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:38,600
Are there really?

409
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:40,060
Indeed.

410
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:52,080
Oh, come on.

411
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:53,900
There's no reason to be so scared.

412
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:57,800
All I have to do is shoot you to origami.

413
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:03,180
Once I've done that, I'll be able to see all kinds of things about what sort of life she's lived in this reality.

414
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:04,680
You have Yud.

415
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:06,020
That's right.

416
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:09,720
Then I don't understand.

417
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:14,040
Why didn't you go ahead and use Yud on origami before, back when she went inverse?

418
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:15,560
Don't be silly.

419
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,740
Do you actually think I could get close enough to her at that point?

420
00:19:18,980 --> 00:19:19,560
Look, whatever.

421
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:20,220
Forget it.

422
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:21,500
Let's do it now.

423
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:24,180
We can still find out why she inversed in this world, right?

424
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:26,020
Kurumi, please.

425
00:19:26,100 --> 00:19:26,840
I need your help.

426
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:30,380
Whatever shall I do with you?

427
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:32,820
Where could it be?

428
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:34,500
I don't get it.

429
00:19:34,660 --> 00:19:36,560
How could I lose my hair clip like this?

430
00:19:37,020 --> 00:19:38,180
Wait, what if...

431
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:41,580
Yes, I knew it!

432
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:42,800
This is where it was!

433
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:44,480
Thank goodness.

434
00:19:45,060 --> 00:19:46,380
I should be more careful.

435
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:47,780
Please, I need your help.

436
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:50,180
But in that case...

437
00:19:50,180 --> 00:19:52,080
Is that Itsuka's voice?

438
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:55,840
Itsuka and...

439
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:56,620
Who?

440
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,640
Origami?

441
00:20:16,220 --> 00:20:16,820
Origami?

442
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:23,000
No, this... I can explain.

443
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:27,380
What's she doing?

444
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:28,940
One way to find out.

445
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:32,280
Let's see, how should I greet you here in this world?

446
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:34,100
Do I say nice to meet you?

447
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:40,100
Though it does seem quite possible that we've already run into each other several times before this moment in time.

448
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:42,260
I will kill you.

449
00:20:46,820 --> 00:21:05,680
Armour? I knew it! I knew you were devil!

450
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:07,040
Satan!

451
00:21:14,220 --> 00:21:16,740
That's a pretty violent way to greet a person.

452
00:21:16,820 --> 00:21:25,820
Don't kill me!

453
00:21:31,820 --> 00:21:34,460
How... how could you do that?

454
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:46,120
What's the meaning of all this?

455
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:49,240
Meaning of what?

456
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:52,160
Itsuka?

457
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:57,820
What on earth are you doing here?

458
00:21:58,500 --> 00:21:59,780
In a place like this?

459
00:21:59,780 --> 00:22:00,280
Oh...

460
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:00,780
Oh...

461
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:06,780
Oh...

462
00:22:06,780 --> 00:22:07,780
Oh...

463
00:22:07,780 --> 00:22:08,780
Oh...

464
00:22:08,780 --> 00:22:09,780
Oh...

465
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:10,780
Oh...

466
00:22:10,780 --> 00:22:11,780
Oh...

467
00:22:11,780 --> 00:22:12,780
Oh...

468
00:22:12,780 --> 00:22:28,020
Oh...

469
00:22:28,020 --> 00:22:36,420
失礼しないこんでた心 君はそっと拾い上げた

470
00:22:36,420 --> 00:22:44,020
繰り返す日々 どうしようもなく紡いた時

471
00:22:44,020 --> 00:22:48,020
ギュッと抱き締めてくれた

472
00:22:48,020 --> 00:22:58,020
ずっとここで 君と二人で 秒空が流れる

473
00:22:58,020 --> 00:23:02,020
星を見続けたい

474
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:07,020
君と最後の約束をしよう

475
00:23:07,020 --> 00:23:13,020
世界から私だけ消えてしまっても

476
00:23:13,020 --> 00:23:18,020
気づかれなくていい このままでいたい

477
00:23:18,020 --> 00:23:26,020
刻まれたこの気持ち いつまでも永遠に

